@title How to Read Your Water Bill
@subtitle A plain guide to your quarterly bill from Tarn Valley Water
@author Tarn Valley Water

Your water bill has a few parts. This guide walks through each one, shows a worked example, and explains what to do if money is tight.

## Your bill at a glance

We send you a bill every 3 months. It adds up three things:

1. **Usage charge**: the water you used, measured by your meter in cubic meters (m3).
2. **Sewer charge**: 80 percent of your usage charge, for taking wastewater away.
3. **Service charge**: a fixed $38.40 every quarter.

kpi Bill arrives | every 3 months | quarterly
kpi Payment due | 21 days | after the issue date
kpi Autopay saving | $2 | off every bill | good

## Usage charges

The more water you use, the higher the price for each extra cubic meter. Your usage is charged in three steps:

table = water used,price per m3; First 30 m3,$1.85; Next 30 m3 (31 to 60),$2.60; Anything above 60 m3,$3.90

The sewer charge is then 80 percent of your usage charge.

### Worked example: a household that used 72 m3

table = part of the bill,how it is worked out,amount; First 30 m3,30 × $1.85,$55.50; Next 30 m3,30 × $2.60,$78.00; Last 12 m3,12 × $3.90,$46.80; **Usage charge**,55.50 + 78.00 + 46.80,**$180.30**; Sewer charge,80% of $180.30,$144.24; Service charge,fixed each quarter,$38.40; **Total**,,**$362.94**

kpi Example total | $362.94 | for 72 m3 in one quarter

## Fixed charges

The service charge is $38.40 every quarter. It stays the same no matter how much water you use, so you will see it on every bill, even in a quarter when you use very little.

## Ways to pay

Payment is due 21 days after the issue date printed on your bill.

- **Online:** [tarnvalleywater.example/pay](https://tarnvalleywater.example/pay)
- **By phone:** 555-0121
- **In person:** our Main Street office, weekdays from 8:30 to 16:30

! Sign up for autopay and we take $2 off every bill.

## If you cannot pay on time

We understand that things happen. If you cannot pay in full, please call us on **555-0133 before your due date**. We will set up a payment plan with you.

!! A late fee of 5 percent is added to bills left unpaid after 30 days, so please call us early.
